WEBVTT

00:30.447 --> 00:31.614
Prisoner 1625!

00:32.157 --> 00:33.366
Get away from him!

00:43.835 --> 00:45.253
Come with me!

01:08.443 --> 01:09.944
The wound is pretty deep.

01:10.445 --> 01:13.615
We're gonna have to keep an eye on him
while he's being treated.

01:13.698 --> 01:15.158
And what about Min Ji-ung?

01:15.241 --> 01:18.161
He wasn't injured. We're keeping him
separated from the attacker.

01:18.244 --> 01:20.246
Let me know
when you're done questioning him.

01:32.092 --> 01:33.510
Choi Ga-yun was my…

01:34.969 --> 01:37.597
She was the only adult
who ever cared about me, sir.

01:39.182 --> 01:41.976
She was gentle, and kind, and…

01:46.314 --> 01:48.024
I'll regret it for the rest of my life.

01:48.650 --> 01:51.111
It will haunt me until the day that I die.

01:52.237 --> 01:56.282
The memory of what I did torments me
every day, and I cannot find peace.

01:56.366 --> 01:58.034
I'm so sorry.

01:58.660 --> 02:00.286
I'm so sorry.

02:06.292 --> 02:07.836
I'm so sorry.

02:08.336 --> 02:09.879
I'm so sorry.

02:10.463 --> 02:12.173
I'm so sorry!

02:12.757 --> 02:14.008
I'm so sorry.

02:50.503 --> 02:52.297
You think you're a saint?

02:52.380 --> 02:55.300
If you hadn't felt anything,
that would make you a psychopath.

02:56.217 --> 02:59.179
I told you. I warned you
that you'll see Cho Gyu-cheol in there.

02:59.262 --> 03:00.638
And inside here,

03:01.139 --> 03:03.141
you'll feel a rage that'll consume you.

03:05.143 --> 03:07.395
It's a rage that will never leave us.

03:07.896 --> 03:09.731
I told you, you had a choice to make.

03:09.814 --> 03:11.900
Either to live as Ga-yun's fiancé,

03:11.983 --> 03:13.985
or to live as an ERPB inspector.

03:19.407 --> 03:20.408
You did well.

03:21.868 --> 03:22.952
You did.

03:23.953 --> 03:25.747
You don't have anything else to say?

03:27.040 --> 03:29.959
You want me to pat you on the back,
and tell you bravo?

03:31.211 --> 03:32.295
Yeah, that'd be nice.

03:33.296 --> 03:34.380
Watch your mouth!

03:39.093 --> 03:41.638
How about a drink? Later on, after work?

03:44.891 --> 03:46.267
Why aren't you answering?

03:48.853 --> 03:52.899
Well, spending my free time with
my father-in-law wasn't top of my list.

03:55.652 --> 03:56.694
You damn punk!

03:57.779 --> 03:58.780
Get out and walk!

03:59.280 --> 04:01.199
It's too late now. We're almost there.

04:01.282 --> 04:04.327
That was pretty mean,
what you just said. Very mean.

04:04.410 --> 04:05.870
I wasn't being mean.

04:05.954 --> 04:08.206
I was just saying
that it wasn't necessarily at the top--

04:08.289 --> 04:10.291
Next time, you take the bus.

04:12.460 --> 04:14.337
Good morning, Minister.

04:14.420 --> 04:17.590
That's enough pleasantries.
How's the drug investigation coming along?

04:17.674 --> 04:19.300
We reached out to the police for help,

04:19.384 --> 04:22.428
and with the school security, we're hoping
to find where they stashed the pills.

04:22.512 --> 04:25.265
And as part
of the new ERPB anti-drug protocols,

04:25.348 --> 04:27.850
we're running mandatory urine tests
in middle schools everywhere.

04:27.934 --> 04:29.060
What about gambling?

04:29.560 --> 04:31.980
We're tracking the IP address
of the online gambling site,

04:32.063 --> 04:34.732
and we're using the tracking system
to find the loan sharks involved.

04:34.816 --> 04:37.819
Gambling is as serious as drugs.
Stay on top of it, okay?

04:37.902 --> 04:39.195
Minister Choi!

04:39.279 --> 04:41.572
-Please, sir! Minister Choi!
-You can't go in there.

04:41.656 --> 04:43.658
-Minister!
-Sir, you're not allowed in here.

04:43.741 --> 04:44.575
Please help me!

04:44.659 --> 04:47.537
If you wanna see the minister,
you have to book an appointment.

04:47.620 --> 04:49.372
I don't have time for an appointment!

04:49.455 --> 04:50.832
-Calm down.
-Minister, please!

04:50.915 --> 04:52.625
-What's going on here?
-Help me!

04:54.168 --> 04:55.295
I'm sorry, sir.

04:55.378 --> 04:57.171
I'm sorry for disturbing you, Mi…

04:57.255 --> 05:00.008
Can you please just take a look
at what I've found?

05:03.219 --> 05:05.221
Look. This is data.

05:05.305 --> 05:06.889
I've done the research myself.

05:07.390 --> 05:11.102
M… It shows all the harm from g… gambling.

05:11.602 --> 05:12.937
And I have also

05:13.771 --> 05:16.649
compiled all the f… formal complaints.

05:16.733 --> 05:18.318
REQUEST TO BLOCK ILLEGAL WEBSITES

05:18.401 --> 05:19.736
There's more. One moment.

05:19.819 --> 05:22.447
Give me a minute.
These are all the medical records.

05:23.239 --> 05:25.950
A… and these are really important.
One moment. Please.

05:26.034 --> 05:28.786
Oh no! Where did I put it?
Where did I put it?

05:29.996 --> 05:32.081
Please take a look. I'm begging you.

05:32.165 --> 05:33.333
HOPE JOURNAL
BY LEE JAE-YUN

05:33.416 --> 05:35.877
Minister Choi, please take a look!

05:37.086 --> 05:39.047
-Have a seat.
-Sir, sit down.

05:39.130 --> 05:40.214
-Please.
-Thanks.

05:41.966 --> 05:44.886
-Careful.
-Hm. Thank you very much.

05:57.065 --> 06:00.360
I'm here because no one will listen to me.
No one believes me.

06:01.527 --> 06:04.405
The authorities refuse to talk to me.
And I get it.

06:04.906 --> 06:07.617
I know that my son's
not completely innocent.

06:08.493 --> 06:11.913
You did the right thing.
Tell me, how can I help you?

06:17.919 --> 06:19.462
It's my fool of a son.

06:21.381 --> 06:24.092
Our sales for the third quarter
increased by 18%

06:24.175 --> 06:25.843
compared to the same period last year.

06:25.927 --> 06:27.220
And our operating profit…

06:27.303 --> 06:29.847
-Hello?
-What the fuck took you so long?

06:30.890 --> 06:32.642
Are you Lee Jae-yun's father?

06:33.267 --> 06:34.977
-I'm sorry, you--
-Shut up!

06:35.478 --> 06:37.188
Answer the fucking question.

06:37.688 --> 06:38.940
Who's speaking?

06:39.023 --> 06:43.152
You don't need to know who I am.
Just pay off your son's fuckin' debt.

06:48.074 --> 06:50.243
Games. I play games.

06:51.494 --> 06:54.247
Games? What, you bought
some in-game items or something?

06:54.330 --> 06:56.499
Okay, so how much money do you owe?

06:56.582 --> 06:59.544
Is it like a hundred, maybe 200,000 won?

07:00.044 --> 07:03.047
Answer your mother!
How much money do you owe?

07:06.134 --> 07:07.176
It's more like

07:07.969 --> 07:09.262
85 million won.

07:12.181 --> 07:15.560
Wh… what? Eight-five million won?
Is that what you said?

07:15.643 --> 07:16.936
Oh God!

07:17.437 --> 07:18.438
I don't know…

07:18.521 --> 07:22.525
What the hell did you do?
What kind of game are you talking about?

07:48.259 --> 07:52.513
TEACH YOU A LESSON

07:54.348 --> 07:55.349
Jae-yun,

07:57.185 --> 07:58.478
your mom and I,

07:59.479 --> 08:00.605
we paid off your debt.

08:01.981 --> 08:03.900
We understand everyone makes mistakes.

08:03.983 --> 08:06.110
But you can't make this mistake twice.

08:06.944 --> 08:08.779
I'm sure you'll do better from now on.

08:09.822 --> 08:12.492
What's important is
that you learn from your mistake…

08:14.660 --> 08:15.828
and never do it again.

08:16.329 --> 08:17.205
Mm-mm.

08:20.666 --> 08:24.253
That's settled, then.
So let's enjoy our meal. Don't cry, okay?

08:27.757 --> 08:29.425
Oh…

08:29.509 --> 08:32.637
It's okay, my baby.
Don't cry. It's over now.

08:44.649 --> 08:47.527
50,000 WON SIGN-UP BONUS
SURPRISE COUPON, CLICK NOW

09:03.668 --> 09:08.005
VIP GAME ROOM
UNLIMITED BONUS EVENT FOR A LIMITED TIME

09:17.265 --> 09:20.142
You damn fool! I don't believe it!

09:20.226 --> 09:22.311
Damn it, Jae-yun. We just paid your debt!

09:22.395 --> 09:24.939
And now, you're gambling again?

09:25.022 --> 09:26.941
Jae-yun, you fool!

09:27.024 --> 09:29.026
-How could you?
-Darling, no! Don't hit him!

09:29.110 --> 09:30.027
Please stop!

09:52.258 --> 09:55.261
Just use it for webtoons
when you're bored, okay?

09:56.304 --> 09:58.180
Just one webtoon.

09:59.015 --> 10:01.267
I am not gonna gamble anymore.

10:24.957 --> 10:26.542
Jesus!

10:26.626 --> 10:29.086
-Sit down, it's none of your business.
-Wait one minute.

10:29.170 --> 10:31.339
Mister, when your kid owes money,

10:31.422 --> 10:33.966
guess who's gotta pay his debt, old man?

10:36.594 --> 10:37.928
Get back to work.

10:38.012 --> 10:40.848
And if your kid screws up, well,

10:40.931 --> 10:42.850
then you have to take a beating.

10:48.564 --> 10:51.233
LETTER OF RESIGNATION

10:55.988 --> 10:56.947
Sir…

10:59.075 --> 11:01.619
I… I really need that redundancy money.

11:05.331 --> 11:06.332
So, you see,

11:06.415 --> 11:07.625
I've tried everything.

11:07.708 --> 11:09.251
I've done all that I could.

11:12.046 --> 11:14.215
I got my son to see a psychiatrist.

11:14.298 --> 11:17.218
They put him on medication
to try to control his addiction.

11:20.304 --> 11:22.640
I even went to see a shaman.

11:23.349 --> 11:24.600
And the police,

11:24.684 --> 11:26.268
I called them a long time ago.

11:26.352 --> 11:27.687
But they said

11:28.646 --> 11:30.690
there was nothing they could do.

11:30.773 --> 11:32.942
Even if they blocked
the IP of the gambling site,

11:33.025 --> 11:34.402
they'd just move on.

11:34.902 --> 11:36.404
Find a new one.

11:36.904 --> 11:41.242
I'm so tired. With all the protocols,
and regulations, and bureaucracy, it's…

11:41.325 --> 11:43.828
It's so disheartening. I mean…

11:44.662 --> 11:47.289
It's taken me over six months
to put all this together.

11:49.291 --> 11:52.128
I kept trying. Time passed and I got…

11:52.211 --> 11:53.963
T… take a look, please.

11:54.922 --> 11:56.590
It's from my son.

11:56.674 --> 11:58.384
He ran away from home.

11:59.593 --> 12:01.846
I don't know if he's alive.

12:04.014 --> 12:05.891
I don't even know why I'm here.

12:06.767 --> 12:10.521
Please forgive me, Minister. I don't know
why I brought all of this stuff.

12:10.604 --> 12:13.065
I just thought that maybe you could…

12:13.149 --> 12:14.692
It's okay, sir.

12:16.360 --> 12:18.779
You don't have to explain anything else.

12:25.327 --> 12:26.370
Good morning.

12:26.454 --> 12:30.124
Please welcome the new transfer student,
Bong Geun-dae, who starts today.

12:30.666 --> 12:31.834
Say hello.

12:32.334 --> 12:33.502
Hi, everyone.

12:33.586 --> 12:36.338
My name is Bong Geun-dae. Good to be here.

12:40.718 --> 12:42.845
Geun-dae, you can sit over there
in front of Seong-bin.

12:43.721 --> 12:45.848
Seong-bin, have you heard
any news from Jae-yun?

12:46.682 --> 12:48.976
-No.
-If you do, let me know, okay?

12:49.477 --> 12:51.020
Okay then, go, Nakwon, go!

12:51.103 --> 12:53.063
Go, Nakwon, go!

12:55.608 --> 12:57.026
-I won! I won!
-Seriously?

12:57.109 --> 12:58.152
I hit the jackpot!

12:58.235 --> 12:59.820
How much did you win? Man!

12:59.904 --> 13:00.988
A million won!

13:01.071 --> 13:02.656
-Really. Take a look!
-Oh my gosh!

13:03.157 --> 13:04.241
So close!

13:04.325 --> 13:07.161
Jackpot! Yeah! I did it! I won!

13:07.244 --> 13:08.329
Yeah!

13:09.955 --> 13:11.999
-You could've done better.
-Come on!

13:12.082 --> 13:14.043
-No! Fuck that! Damn it!
-Shit!

13:14.126 --> 13:15.961
-Lose.
-I'm done!

13:16.045 --> 13:17.838
-Yes! I won!
-Lose.

13:21.550 --> 13:25.721
Fuck! My mom's gonna kill me
if she finds out I lost. I'm fucked!

13:25.805 --> 13:27.348
Come on! Please!

13:27.431 --> 13:29.058
-Lose.
-Shit!

13:29.141 --> 13:30.434
What the hell?

13:30.518 --> 13:33.103
What the fuck are you looking at,
newbie? Move over.

13:33.854 --> 13:35.648
The reports and statistics confirm

13:35.731 --> 13:39.109
that most online gambling centers
use teenage labor and operators.

13:39.193 --> 13:42.488
The Bureau recently participated
in several gambling center busts,

13:42.571 --> 13:44.406
and over 50% arrested were minors.

13:44.490 --> 13:46.909
A nine-year-old? You're kidding?
A nine-year-old!

13:46.992 --> 13:48.494
This isn't just addiction.

13:48.577 --> 13:50.955
The kids end up owing thousands
to gangsters and loan sharks.

13:51.038 --> 13:52.957
Thousands? It's a lot more than that!

13:53.040 --> 13:55.918
And some of them
owe millions of won. Millions!

13:56.001 --> 13:59.255
The latest reports show that many of
these kids end up running away from home,

13:59.338 --> 14:00.256
just like Jae-yun.

14:00.339 --> 14:03.634
Gambling is one thing. The other crimes
related to it are also very serious.

14:03.717 --> 14:05.427
Most of it is to pay off their debts.

14:05.511 --> 14:07.930
It's time that we put a stop to this.

14:08.013 --> 14:11.892
But, sir, we can't do this on our own.
We need help from the police.

14:11.976 --> 14:13.102
Not just the police.

14:13.185 --> 14:15.521
Always remember,
"It takes a village to raise a child."

14:15.604 --> 14:18.482
We need to work with all the ministries.
It's the only way.

14:19.692 --> 14:21.235
And if they don't cooperate,

14:21.318 --> 14:23.946
I'll drag them out
by the scruff of their necks.

14:24.029 --> 14:26.198
Aren't they a bit above your pay grade?

14:26.282 --> 14:28.117
They'd be wrong to mess with me.

14:30.703 --> 14:31.912
Have a nice day, sir.

14:38.335 --> 14:39.295
Lose.

14:40.004 --> 14:43.966
So, where did you come from?
Me? Well, I came from my home.

14:44.049 --> 14:46.176
Dumbass! I mean from what school?

14:47.136 --> 14:48.721
-Guun High.
-Whoa!

14:48.804 --> 14:52.433
-Yes! I got it, I won! Jackpot, baby!
-What did you win? How much?

14:52.516 --> 14:54.894
-How much?
-Holy shit. I got a million!

14:54.977 --> 14:56.979
-A million!
-You won a million?

14:57.062 --> 14:58.439
What are you guys playing?

14:58.522 --> 15:00.274
What's that? Dinner's on me, guys.

15:00.357 --> 15:01.859
You bet I'm going!

15:01.942 --> 15:04.278
Seong-bin hit the jackpot!
Dinner's on him, motherfuckers!

15:04.361 --> 15:05.946
A million won!

15:06.030 --> 15:07.156
Jackpot. That's right!

15:07.239 --> 15:09.450
-Barbecue beef!
-I want hot pot soup!

15:09.533 --> 15:10.701
-Lobster!
-Shrimp!

15:10.784 --> 15:12.620
-Yeah!
-I'll have some fried chicken!

15:14.413 --> 15:17.249
Okay, then.
Maybe I'll have some spicy beef.

15:17.833 --> 15:20.878
-I'm going all in, I'm feeling lucky here.
-Hang on a sec.

15:21.378 --> 15:24.298
Be patient. If you go all in,
we can lose this winning streak. Trust me.

15:24.381 --> 15:26.508
Bro, I trust you as far as I can lift you.

15:27.009 --> 15:29.136
Bro, it's "Trust you
as far as I can throw you."

15:29.219 --> 15:30.429
It's my last card.

15:34.600 --> 15:36.393
Yes! Yes!

15:36.477 --> 15:38.437
Whoo! Yes!

15:38.520 --> 15:40.898
-Hey!
-Oh my goodness!

15:41.398 --> 15:43.067
Guys, sorry, but what is it?

15:43.150 --> 15:44.485
What are you guys playing?

15:44.568 --> 15:45.945
I told you. It's a game.

15:46.028 --> 15:50.115
But isn't it actually gambling?
I mean, you win money and make bets.

15:50.199 --> 15:51.659
Gambling is scary, you know.

15:51.742 --> 15:53.786
This is just a game.
A game where you make some money.

15:54.370 --> 15:56.747
Okay, but to play, you use your own money?

15:56.830 --> 15:59.083
Who would use their own money?
Use the bonus they give you.

15:59.166 --> 16:01.961
When Seong-bin signed up,
he used his free bonus

16:02.461 --> 16:03.837
and he got a new graphics card.

16:03.921 --> 16:06.173
Graphics card?
Those can be pretty expensive.

16:06.256 --> 16:07.132
Wanna get one?

16:08.133 --> 16:09.134
I can show you.

16:10.094 --> 16:11.178
Yeah.

16:11.720 --> 16:12.805
Here's how you start.

16:12.888 --> 16:15.766
If you use my ID as a referral,
you'll get 50 grand.

16:15.849 --> 16:17.309
Free cash.

16:17.393 --> 16:19.395
Free? Are you really sure?

16:20.062 --> 16:23.649
All right, smart-ass. Give me that.

16:23.732 --> 16:26.986
Okay, so first off, we sign up.

16:27.069 --> 16:28.779
Then you put in your password,

16:28.862 --> 16:32.074
and for the code, we use sungbin99. There.

16:32.157 --> 16:34.243
Bingo. You got 50 Gs.

16:34.326 --> 16:36.912
You're a beginner,
so start easy with Odd and Even.

16:37.413 --> 16:39.540
-What's that?
-Go on, just chose one.

16:39.623 --> 16:40.916
I'll go with odd?

16:41.000 --> 16:42.126
-Do it.
-Okay.

16:43.752 --> 16:45.254
-Win!
-Wow!

16:45.337 --> 16:48.048
-Whoa!
-Can you believe it, asshole?

16:48.132 --> 16:49.258
Look at that!

16:49.967 --> 16:51.010
Even.

16:53.554 --> 16:55.055
Hey, what's your bid?

16:55.556 --> 16:59.601
This guy. First, someone approaches you.
We call them recruiters.

16:59.685 --> 17:02.438
This is Seong-bin,
and he works on grooming new users.

17:02.521 --> 17:04.189
At the beginning, he talks it up.

17:04.273 --> 17:08.152
He talks about easy money, and he really
grabs your attention and curiosity.

17:08.235 --> 17:09.862
However, if you don't gamble,

17:09.945 --> 17:13.741
they exclude you from their circle
and isolate you. Then, you're an outcast.

17:13.824 --> 17:16.910
They use the word "game" instead
of "gambling." It seems more acceptable.

17:16.994 --> 17:20.622
So, the next part of the plan
is to have Deputy Bong lose money?

17:20.706 --> 17:23.250
There's something
I don't really understand.

17:23.333 --> 17:25.919
'Cause it's basically just math.
The gambling…

17:26.003 --> 17:30.507
If you've done basic middle school math
and a little simple statistics, well,

17:30.591 --> 17:33.552
it kinda seems to me
that you can't really lose.

17:33.635 --> 17:35.971
Hm. Maybe.

17:36.055 --> 17:38.015
I mean, you don't have to lose.

17:38.098 --> 17:40.059
If you can win, win!

17:40.142 --> 17:42.770
And what do I do with the money I win?

17:42.853 --> 17:44.438
Why not keep it, like a bonus?

17:45.481 --> 17:46.356
No…

17:46.440 --> 17:47.733
You don't believe me?

17:48.317 --> 17:49.735
-So?
-Should I believe you?

17:50.360 --> 17:52.154
Well, come on, if you won it yourself…

17:58.452 --> 17:59.995
Well, okay, then.

18:05.250 --> 18:08.212
-How much is the graphics card?
-Are you sure this is okay?

18:08.295 --> 18:10.255
Yeah, I trust him. He'll be fine.

18:28.107 --> 18:30.025
What do I do with the money I win?

18:30.109 --> 18:32.778
Why not keep it, like a bonus?

18:33.695 --> 18:35.739
Why not keep it, like a bonus?

18:48.877 --> 18:50.045
Win!

18:51.547 --> 18:52.965
Win!

18:54.299 --> 18:55.551
Win!

18:56.844 --> 18:58.137
Win!

18:59.346 --> 19:00.973
Win! Win! Win!

19:14.820 --> 19:15.779
Lose.

19:17.739 --> 19:18.782
Lose.

19:20.576 --> 19:21.451
Lose.

19:22.661 --> 19:23.704
Lose.

19:24.329 --> 19:25.706
Lose.

19:45.475 --> 19:48.312
YOUR BALANCE HAS RUN OUT
RECHARGE

19:54.651 --> 19:56.028
Look at this dude!

19:57.696 --> 20:00.032
Whoa! You were up all night, right?

20:00.741 --> 20:01.658
Did you win?

20:02.326 --> 20:03.368
No, I lost.

20:03.452 --> 20:04.411
How much?

20:05.787 --> 20:06.747
A million.

20:06.830 --> 20:09.499
Are you nuts? I told you
not to use your own money!

20:11.168 --> 20:12.753
What now?

20:12.836 --> 20:14.588
What are you gonna do?
You wanna win, right?

20:15.756 --> 20:16.965
How can I win it back?

20:17.549 --> 20:20.677
Have you heard
about Martingale's betting strategy?

20:21.553 --> 20:25.057
My bro Martingale came up with this
miracle method where you can never lose.

20:26.141 --> 20:28.977
It's foolproof. You double your bet
when you lose.

20:29.061 --> 20:31.772
If you lose 100, you bet 200.

20:31.855 --> 20:34.524
Two hundred? Four hundred. You lose 400?

20:35.108 --> 20:37.236
-Then I bet eight.
-You got it.

20:37.319 --> 20:40.239
The odds are that you'll win.
You just need to win once.

20:40.322 --> 20:43.325
Yeah, one time is all I need
to get it back.

20:43.408 --> 20:46.286
Exactly! It's a really simple,
foolproof strategy.

20:46.370 --> 20:48.455
Once you have the money,
you can never lose.

20:49.665 --> 20:51.583
Bong, all is not lost, my friend.

20:52.626 --> 20:54.544
I know someone who can lend you that cash.

20:55.671 --> 20:56.630
Want some money?

20:58.799 --> 21:00.550
There's no need to overthink it.

21:02.010 --> 21:03.345
Hey, man, it's me.

21:03.428 --> 21:05.347
I've got a friend who needs cash.

21:05.973 --> 21:07.474
Yeah, about a million won.

21:08.850 --> 21:10.060
You're good to go.

21:10.143 --> 21:11.561
But he wants some insurance.

21:11.645 --> 21:13.397
-Some what?
-It's no biggie.

21:13.480 --> 21:14.648
He needs your parents' number.

21:14.731 --> 21:15.899
My parents' phone number?

21:15.983 --> 21:19.194
Don't worry, it's a formality.
Who cares? You're gonna win.

21:19.278 --> 21:20.279
Martingale, remember?

21:26.451 --> 21:27.452
800,000 WON DEPOSITED

21:27.536 --> 21:29.746
I thought you said
he would lend me a million?

21:29.830 --> 21:31.540
But there's only 800.

21:31.623 --> 21:35.377
The guy needs to make a living, right?
He takes a 20% cut.

21:39.131 --> 21:41.049
The interest is 3% a day.

21:41.133 --> 21:43.302
So for one million won, that's 30,000.

21:43.385 --> 21:45.595
The next day's interest isn't one million.

21:45.679 --> 21:48.265
It's 3% on top of 1,030,000.

21:48.348 --> 21:50.559
It's called compound interest.

21:51.059 --> 21:52.394
So after one month,

21:52.477 --> 21:53.770
that 800,000,

21:53.854 --> 21:58.567
it becomes 2,427,243 won!

21:58.650 --> 22:02.362
And after a hundred days,
it becomes more than 19 million won.

22:04.364 --> 22:09.077
And then it becomes over 48 million won.
It's simply unbelievable in just one year.

22:09.161 --> 22:13.165
Don't stress, Deputy.
You did a good job. It's all right, okay?

22:13.248 --> 22:15.375
You did exactly what we wanted you to do.

22:15.459 --> 22:19.004
You're up to your neck in debt,
which means they'll be coming for you.

22:19.671 --> 22:21.340
Don't cry.

22:26.303 --> 22:27.179
Hello?

22:27.721 --> 22:28.930
You're Geun-dae's mom?

22:29.639 --> 22:32.017
-What?
-Answer the fucking question!

22:32.100 --> 22:34.644
Why would I be Bong's mom,
and who do you think you are?!

22:34.728 --> 22:36.229
Who's on the phone, Mrs. Bong?

22:36.313 --> 22:38.398
-My mom?
-Quiet! Geun-dae's mom is talking!

22:41.109 --> 22:43.153
Hello. This is Bong Geun-dae's mother.

22:43.779 --> 22:46.156
You need to pay off
your dumbass son's debt.

22:46.239 --> 22:48.992
Has he been gambling again?
How much does he owe you?

22:49.076 --> 22:51.912
Twenty million.
Your kid's got some serious balls.

22:54.039 --> 22:55.874
Hey, lady? You better pay me back fast.

22:55.957 --> 22:57.209
-It's okay.
-I'm so sorry.

22:57.292 --> 22:59.753
By tomorrow,
he'll owe 600,000 in interest alone.

22:59.836 --> 23:03.840
I don't have that much money. I can't
do it. I can't keep paying his debts.

23:03.924 --> 23:07.010
If I keep paying, then my whole family
pays for his stupidity!

23:07.094 --> 23:10.055
Do whatever you want. I've given up
on Geun-dae. Murder him for all I care.

23:13.100 --> 23:16.520
Damn it, damn it!
He's calling me again. He's calling. Shit!

23:18.522 --> 23:19.523
So, what do we do?

23:19.606 --> 23:23.402
We know the recruiters are small fry,
and we know this operation is cash heavy,

23:23.485 --> 23:25.946
so we follow the money,
it'll lead us to the top.

23:28.198 --> 23:30.909
Our dear colleague here,
he lost pretty big last night.

23:30.992 --> 23:32.744
They'll send someone to collect.

23:33.245 --> 23:34.579
Then, we'll follow them.

23:35.664 --> 23:37.416
And they'll lead us to

23:37.958 --> 23:38.917
the people on top.

23:41.128 --> 23:43.296
It's okay. Don't cry, Deputy.

23:43.380 --> 23:44.256
Okay.

23:45.340 --> 23:47.426
NAKWON HIGH SCHOOL

23:50.887 --> 23:54.724
No sign of the gang members.
You're keeping a close eye on me, right?

23:56.351 --> 23:58.812
Yeah, don't worry.
I'm looking at you from the van.

24:02.149 --> 24:03.191
Hm.

24:07.279 --> 24:10.532
Oh, damn it. I really picked
the wrong spot to be waiting at.

24:14.327 --> 24:16.288
DELICIOUS GIMBAP, TTEOKBOKKI,
TWIGIM, SUNDAE

24:32.345 --> 24:34.598
Ah, welcome girls.

24:34.681 --> 24:36.766
-One serving today.
-Make it two!

24:36.850 --> 24:39.311
This is all I have left.
Don't worry. I'll be generous!

24:39.394 --> 24:42.981
-Thank you! It looks delicious.
-My pleasure. Enjoy.

24:43.064 --> 24:45.650
-Thank you so much!
-Aw.

24:45.734 --> 24:47.652
-Thank you!
-Dig in and enjoy.

24:47.736 --> 24:49.571
Ma'am! Can I have one, too, please?

24:49.654 --> 24:52.282
-Of course.
-Can you add some extra sauce?

24:52.365 --> 24:53.867
-There.
-Thank you!

24:53.950 --> 24:55.785
My pleasure. Enjoy your meal.

25:04.503 --> 25:05.420
Oh no!

25:07.214 --> 25:08.089
Mmm.

25:08.715 --> 25:09.674
Hm?!

25:22.771 --> 25:24.940
Unlock your phones,
hand them to me. All of you.

25:28.193 --> 25:29.402
Come on!

25:31.530 --> 25:33.448
Move it, move it, move it!

25:34.241 --> 25:35.617
INSPECTOR IM HAN-RIM

25:35.700 --> 25:38.119
Hand over these fucking phones! Faster!

25:41.164 --> 25:43.708
Hey, kid! Give me your damn phone.

25:44.376 --> 25:48.046
Yeah, it's… it's just
the print recognition. It's not working.

25:48.129 --> 25:49.422
Give it!

25:56.471 --> 25:58.598
-Oh, s… sorry.
-That's gross, man!

25:58.682 --> 26:00.767
-Let me open this.
-What the fuck?

26:02.602 --> 26:03.979
I lost my phone!

26:05.063 --> 26:06.982
I dropped it. It fell on the road.

26:07.065 --> 26:10.277
For fuck's sake, kid.
What kinda shit is that, you dumb fuck?

26:10.360 --> 26:12.320
I'm sorry. It's my fault.

26:23.290 --> 26:27.794
INSPECTOR IM HAN-RIM

26:27.877 --> 26:30.797
I don't believe it. I saw him.
I was watching him from over there.

26:30.880 --> 26:32.882
I had him in my sights. What the hell?

26:32.966 --> 26:34.759
He's not picking up!

26:34.843 --> 26:36.970
Let's get that camera footage. Come on.

26:39.973 --> 26:42.934
My money! I want my fucking money.

26:43.935 --> 26:46.646
You pay me what you owe me
or you're fucking dead.

26:46.730 --> 26:48.481
Your parents won't pay your debts anymore,

26:48.565 --> 26:51.693
so you're gonna have to find a way
to earn it and pay me back.

26:51.776 --> 26:54.487
Take this. Take it!

26:55.113 --> 26:57.741
Go to that ice-cream parlor
and grab the cash, okay?

26:59.200 --> 27:00.452
Go!

27:24.059 --> 27:25.226
Well done.

27:29.648 --> 27:31.733
You did good. Get in.

27:39.240 --> 27:40.617
If you don't do it,

27:41.368 --> 27:42.661
I'll kill you instead.

27:43.244 --> 27:44.621
You understand, kid?

27:45.413 --> 27:47.666
-I'm not sure I can do it
-Hold on tight.

27:49.000 --> 27:51.878
-Hey! No! I can't do it. Don't make me!
-Do it! You wanna die?

27:51.961 --> 27:55.090
Get the fuck out there, kid!
I said get the fuck out and do it.

27:55.173 --> 27:57.467
-Please!
-You stupid fucking idiot.

27:57.550 --> 27:58.635
Oh!

28:06.309 --> 28:08.687
Ow! What the hell?

28:08.770 --> 28:11.690
-Are you all right?
-What the fuck is your problem?

28:11.773 --> 28:13.858
-Come here! Hey, you!
-What's going on?

28:28.998 --> 28:29.833
Damn it.

28:32.293 --> 28:36.047
Run the plates through the system,
and check that van on security cameras.

28:36.131 --> 28:38.675
I'll go see traffic control
and see if they can help us.

28:38.758 --> 28:39.592
Yes, sir.

28:44.431 --> 28:45.890
Get hold of yourself.

28:45.974 --> 28:47.183
We don't have the time.

28:47.267 --> 28:48.852
This is all my fault.

28:50.186 --> 28:53.314
I lost sight of Deputy Bong
all because of some damn tteokbokki!

28:53.815 --> 28:56.568
What if something bad happens to him
because of me?

28:58.570 --> 29:00.155
Sergeant Im Han-rim!

29:00.238 --> 29:01.990
Yes, Sergeant, you're a soldier.

29:03.700 --> 29:05.702
You can make up for your mistake.

29:07.328 --> 29:09.038
But if you give up now, you'll fail.

29:11.499 --> 29:12.417
Understood?

29:13.418 --> 29:14.711
Understood, sir!

29:18.548 --> 29:19.674
Let's do this.

29:25.430 --> 29:27.766
Damn it! Where the hell are those guys?

29:27.849 --> 29:30.643
-This is un-fucking-believable.
-Fuck this!

29:30.727 --> 29:33.271
Hey! I told you to keep your eyes closed!

29:41.738 --> 29:44.324
Easy! Please don't hurt me.

29:44.824 --> 29:46.659
Whoa, wait a second, hey!

29:46.743 --> 29:48.369
-Hang on, wait!
-Hey, boss!

29:48.453 --> 29:50.914
You fucking idiots
treating yourself to a nice snack?

29:50.997 --> 29:52.040
Sorry, boss.

29:52.123 --> 29:54.375
You expect me
to take care of these school kids myself?

29:54.459 --> 29:56.127
-Move it!
-Sorry, sir!

29:56.211 --> 29:58.463
-Get your shit together.
-Yes, sir!

29:59.172 --> 30:01.216
I'm surrounded by idiots!

30:01.299 --> 30:02.884
-Have a good night, sir.
-Good night, sir.

30:03.968 --> 30:06.971
Hey. This kid is new. Teach him the ropes,
and then put him to work tonight.

30:07.055 --> 30:08.598
Will do. Yes, sir.

30:09.933 --> 30:11.267
Come with me, dumbass.

30:11.351 --> 30:13.269
Oh! Sorry, that's my bag.

30:13.978 --> 30:15.063
That's my bag!

30:15.146 --> 30:17.190
Quiet! Keep moving and shut up.

30:20.443 --> 30:21.444
Oh.

30:23.446 --> 30:25.073
-Sit down.
-What?

30:25.156 --> 30:26.533
I said, sit down!

30:28.159 --> 30:31.037
Listen up.
You gotta get through all this tonight.

30:31.746 --> 30:34.040
You see? All these numbers
done by tonight.

30:34.123 --> 30:35.750
You send a text message to all of them.

30:36.334 --> 30:37.293
Got it?

30:38.211 --> 30:40.088
-Yeah.
-You look dumb as fuck.

30:40.171 --> 30:42.173
Damn it. Waste of my time.

30:48.847 --> 30:50.932
TEXT RECIPIENT LIST

30:59.107 --> 31:00.441
IT'S BONG, I'VE BEEN TAKEN

31:02.110 --> 31:04.612
-Oh! You're Jae--
-Shh!

31:06.531 --> 31:08.408
There are cameras everywhere watching us.

31:10.326 --> 31:12.036
They're watching the monitors too.

31:12.120 --> 31:14.581
Hey! Who the fuck is talking back there?

31:14.664 --> 31:16.374
Oh!

31:21.212 --> 31:23.631
What the fuck
do we have here, ladies? Huh?

31:23.715 --> 31:27.218
You dumb son of a bitch. Did I give you
permission to talk? Dumbass?

31:28.136 --> 31:29.846
Oh!

31:29.929 --> 31:32.807
You really are starting
to piss me off, asshole.

31:33.808 --> 31:36.019
Fuckhead? You hear me?

31:36.102 --> 31:37.770
Are you fucking listening to me?

31:37.854 --> 31:41.149
You're dumb as fuck,
and stop acting like this is hurting you.

31:41.232 --> 31:43.109
Don't fuckin' annoy me, okay?

31:48.656 --> 31:49.699
50,000 WON BONUS

31:49.782 --> 31:51.200
MESSAGE HAS BEEN SENT

31:51.284 --> 31:53.453
What the fuck is happening? Fix this shit!

31:53.536 --> 31:56.247
Get the hell out of here, you idiots.
You guys are fucking useless!

31:56.331 --> 31:57.832
Get the hell out of here!

32:00.376 --> 32:02.462
Hey, you fucking bitches,
we got work to do.

32:03.212 --> 32:05.256
-Damn this shit!
-What's wrong with the boss?

32:05.340 --> 32:07.508
There's a problem
with the Cambodian server.

32:07.592 --> 32:10.887
Looks like it's lagging 'cause the fucking
traffic spiked all at the same time.

32:10.970 --> 32:13.431
-We're getting complaints nonstop.
-Fuck, yeah, I know.

32:13.932 --> 32:16.809
-What's that got to do with us?
-Why the fuck's he pissed with us?

32:19.395 --> 32:20.438
Is he sleeping?

32:20.521 --> 32:23.358
My day is already a fucking mess
and this punk takes a nap?

32:23.441 --> 32:26.486
Okay, you wanna sleep,
I'll help you sleep, bitch.

32:27.987 --> 32:28.821
Please, no.

32:30.573 --> 32:34.452
-You want a fucking break?
-Wait! Don't! I can help. I can do it.

32:34.535 --> 32:37.205
I think I can do it.
I can help. I think I can do it.

32:38.414 --> 32:41.167
-Do what?
-I can fix the Cambodian server. Yeah.

32:41.250 --> 32:44.170
I'm pretty sure that I can fix it
by setting up a reverse proxy relay.

32:44.253 --> 32:46.673
-You can figure this out?
-Yeah. I'm good with computers.

32:46.756 --> 32:48.007
I love computers.

32:49.467 --> 32:51.803
-Well, then, come with us.
-Yeah.

33:06.526 --> 33:07.986
This way. Move it.

33:08.069 --> 33:10.446
The server keeps fucking crashing!

33:10.530 --> 33:11.948
Boss, look what we found.

33:12.573 --> 33:13.783
Who the hell is that?

33:13.866 --> 33:16.160
I think you should talk to this kid.

33:18.538 --> 33:19.455
Ah.

33:20.707 --> 33:22.583
Hm. Uh…

33:23.584 --> 33:25.378
So you see, the thing about lag is

33:25.461 --> 33:28.589
we need to find a way to reduce
the amount of traffic on the server.

33:28.673 --> 33:31.467
So I'm setting up
what we call a reverse proxy,

33:31.551 --> 33:34.929
which is kind of like a gatekeeper
that sits in front of the server.

33:35.430 --> 33:36.723
Okay. Do it.

33:37.598 --> 33:40.184
If it doesn't work,
I'm gonna gouge your eyes out

33:40.268 --> 33:42.645
to make sure you don't see anything else.

33:43.479 --> 33:44.313
Okay?

33:44.897 --> 33:45.857
Yeah…

34:07.378 --> 34:10.465
Well, this guy's
not as stupid as he looks.

34:11.841 --> 34:13.384
-Here you go. Eat up.
-Thanks.

34:13.468 --> 34:15.970
Dig in. Enjoy yourself. Go ahead.

34:18.765 --> 34:20.641
Here. Have some water too.

34:28.483 --> 34:29.484
Shit. He's sleeping again.

34:29.567 --> 34:32.070
Seriously, this guy.

34:37.575 --> 34:40.203
-What's wrong with him?
-He just keeps falling asleep.

34:41.287 --> 34:42.163
Hey?

34:43.122 --> 34:46.667
Can you believe this kid?
Fucking slacker. Jesus.

34:47.543 --> 34:49.420
-Get him out of here
-Yes, sir.

34:50.421 --> 34:52.173
Hey kid, come on, get up!

34:56.052 --> 34:58.262
It's okay.
Don't worry about it. He's fine.

35:07.438 --> 35:09.398
It was registered under a fake name.

35:09.482 --> 35:12.318
We lost track of it on CCTV
at the Susaek intersection.

35:12.902 --> 35:16.447
We were able to track down his phone,
but we can't open it.

35:19.242 --> 35:21.744
-And the other kids?
-Inspector Han-rim is still looking.

35:21.828 --> 35:22.662
She will.

35:22.745 --> 35:24.413
Get your ass in here. Sit down.

35:25.581 --> 35:27.333
I told you to sit down!

35:27.416 --> 35:31.045
I swear, I'm telling the truth. All I did
was encourage the others to play the game.

35:31.129 --> 35:33.172
I have no idea where they are at all.

35:35.591 --> 35:38.553
Show us. Which site
are these bastards operating?

35:40.346 --> 35:41.722
Show it to me!

35:45.685 --> 35:46.686
This one here.

35:48.980 --> 35:51.774
I'll head to the cybercrime unit,
track down their address.

36:13.462 --> 36:14.630
What are you doing?

36:29.061 --> 36:31.480
MUSANGOL

36:35.568 --> 36:38.404
Musang… Musangol Mansin Aegi.

36:40.406 --> 36:43.034
Musangol Mansin Aegi?
What the hell is that?

36:43.534 --> 36:45.703
The VIP banner
is blinking slower than the others.

36:45.786 --> 36:49.916
You can see it there, sir. Morse code.
Each blink corresponds to a letter.

36:49.999 --> 36:51.459
Bong Geun-dae's location is…

36:52.793 --> 36:53.794
He's located at…

36:55.087 --> 36:56.881
Musangol Mansin Aegi.

37:05.514 --> 37:09.393
MUSANGOL MANSIN AEGI SHRINE

37:26.327 --> 37:27.578
The whole place is empty.

37:28.162 --> 37:29.497
We must have got it wrong.

37:29.580 --> 37:31.249
No, something's missing.

37:31.332 --> 37:33.459
What can be missing? There's nothing here!

37:35.878 --> 37:37.922
What if he saw this place
from another building?

37:58.651 --> 37:59.568
Get the gate.

38:02.863 --> 38:05.241
Man, there's no smoking here.
Take it outside.

38:05.324 --> 38:07.285
You're fucking with my lungs.

38:07.368 --> 38:08.703
Bong Geun-dae!

38:10.204 --> 38:11.580
Bong Geun-dae!

38:12.081 --> 38:15.209
-Who the hell are you? Huh?
-I said no killing. Don't forget!

38:15.293 --> 38:17.295
Get outta here! What the fuck?!

38:18.796 --> 38:21.257
Hey! Take this, okay?

38:21.841 --> 38:25.344
You can share it with him.
Here. This is for you.

38:27.388 --> 38:28.514
What the fuck?

38:29.015 --> 38:30.099
Bong Geun-dae?

38:31.183 --> 38:32.560
Have you seen Geun-dae?

38:32.643 --> 38:34.854
Guy with small,
pretty gray eyes that sparkle?

38:34.937 --> 38:36.647
He looks like a computer geek,

38:37.481 --> 38:39.150
but if you look closely, he's kinda cute.

38:39.233 --> 38:42.403
He's tall, and he looks super smart.

38:42.486 --> 38:43.487
Fuck you, lady!

38:47.366 --> 38:48.451
Answer me!

38:49.327 --> 38:50.328
"Kinda cute," huh?

38:51.579 --> 38:54.206
It's a girl.
She must be somebody's sister.

38:55.708 --> 38:57.960
Jeez, man, that's embarrassing!

38:58.044 --> 39:01.464
Han-rim, listen to me.
Don't let your emotions get the bett…

39:03.007 --> 39:04.050
She put her hair up.

39:04.133 --> 39:05.926
Guys, answer me.

39:06.010 --> 39:08.179
-We're not here to kill.
-No answer?

39:08.262 --> 39:10.056
Just focus on the "kinda cute" guy.

39:10.639 --> 39:12.641
-Im Han-rim!
-Still no answer.

39:12.725 --> 39:14.018
This is a fucking joke!

39:15.019 --> 39:15.936
Fucking bitch!

39:27.656 --> 39:28.699
Hey, Han-rim?

39:34.205 --> 39:35.206
You're dead!

39:43.506 --> 39:45.716
Who the fuck are you?!

39:49.970 --> 39:50.805
Shit!

40:04.819 --> 40:06.487
Hey, come on, what are you doing?

40:07.655 --> 40:08.948
Pivot!

40:10.199 --> 40:11.200
Son of a bitch!

40:28.467 --> 40:29.593
Bong Geun-dae?!

40:29.677 --> 40:31.554
-You're being way too emotional.
-Geun-dae!

40:31.637 --> 40:33.806
-Don't you think so?
-I'm over here!

40:56.203 --> 40:57.371
Are you okay?

40:57.455 --> 40:59.165
-Did they hurt you?
-No.

41:00.916 --> 41:01.834
I'm fine.

41:03.252 --> 41:05.588
Inspector, take it easy on him!

41:05.671 --> 41:07.631
I'm okay. Don't worry about me.

41:08.549 --> 41:10.801
Go upstairs. You'll find their boss.

41:12.761 --> 41:14.054
But first…

41:18.100 --> 41:20.478
Im Han-rim, take care of them
and Deputy Bong.

41:21.812 --> 41:24.565
He's tall, and his eyes
do sparkle. Very cute.

41:29.320 --> 41:30.529
You're okay now.

41:43.334 --> 41:44.668
Hey!

41:45.544 --> 41:47.087
I wanna talk to your boss.

41:48.589 --> 41:49.798
Your boss?

41:49.882 --> 41:52.176
Your boss? I wanna talk to him!

42:10.819 --> 42:13.113
I guess you're the guys
who know how to fight?

42:27.044 --> 42:28.337
Tell me where I…

42:29.880 --> 42:31.048
Good night.

43:14.258 --> 43:15.843
Stop!

43:16.760 --> 43:19.346
-The fuck?
-Don't run, you damn fool.

43:20.264 --> 43:22.182
Why are you making this difficult?

43:34.445 --> 43:36.614
Shit!

43:38.324 --> 43:39.491
You son of a bitch!

43:49.877 --> 43:51.045
Get out.

43:56.342 --> 43:58.510
Why did you make me do that, huh?

44:09.146 --> 44:10.648
No! Don't hurt me, please!

44:15.486 --> 44:16.862
I'm begging you. Spare me.

44:20.074 --> 44:23.160
Okay, you're right.
There's been enough violence already.

44:23.243 --> 44:24.286
I could do that. Hm?

44:25.037 --> 44:27.414
But you realize I can't do it for free?

44:28.082 --> 44:29.625
You've committed too many crimes.

44:30.125 --> 44:31.210
You like games, yeah?

44:31.293 --> 44:32.419
Let's play a game.

44:32.503 --> 44:35.214
Let's make a deal.
I'll let you go if you win. Sound good?

44:36.298 --> 44:38.258
-What do you wanna play?
-Have you seen Squid Game?

44:38.342 --> 44:40.761
If you win, you live.
If you lose, I smack you.

44:40.844 --> 44:42.054
Just once. What do you say?

44:44.056 --> 44:45.891
-Well--
-Rock, paper, scissors.

44:46.767 --> 44:48.727
Rock, paper, scissors.

44:57.528 --> 44:58.779
Okay, let's try again.

44:58.862 --> 45:01.573
Rock, paper, scissors. Hm?

45:08.706 --> 45:11.417
-All right? Again. Rock, paper, scissors.
-I can't!

45:12.376 --> 45:14.128
No, no, no, no, wait, please!

45:14.211 --> 45:15.629
Wait? Why?

45:15.713 --> 45:17.673
Because I'll just keep

45:18.173 --> 45:19.717
losing no matter what I do.

45:20.843 --> 45:22.720
What d'you think
you've been doing to those kids?

45:23.554 --> 45:27.266
You're guilty of so many crimes.
Crime one, having them lose their friends.

45:29.393 --> 45:31.395
Then, having them lose their families.

45:32.479 --> 45:34.231
You also took away from them

45:34.982 --> 45:36.692
the joy of going to school.

45:37.735 --> 45:39.319
You're also guilty of

45:39.820 --> 45:41.822
breaking their parents' hearts.

45:44.908 --> 45:45.743
Wakey, wakey.

45:47.453 --> 45:50.164
We're not done yet. Are you ready?

45:51.290 --> 45:52.207
Rock.

45:53.083 --> 45:54.793
Paper.

45:54.877 --> 45:56.044
Scissors.

45:58.589 --> 45:59.923
Rock!

46:40.047 --> 46:42.049
Here! Jae-yun.

46:46.553 --> 46:48.055
Hey. Jae-yun.

46:49.681 --> 46:50.682
Jae-yun.

46:54.228 --> 46:55.270
Hey there.

46:56.939 --> 46:59.024
Help me, please.

47:01.568 --> 47:03.821
You're gonna be okay.

47:05.531 --> 47:06.824
You're safe now.

47:10.285 --> 47:11.370
We got you.

47:30.472 --> 47:31.640
Whoa. Over there.

47:31.723 --> 47:32.766
Look! Look!

47:34.017 --> 47:35.394
You're fine. It's okay.

47:37.062 --> 47:38.021
What's up with him?

47:38.105 --> 47:40.274
It's the stress.
Imagine what he went through.

47:40.858 --> 47:42.234
It's all coming back to him.

47:42.317 --> 47:44.903
In any case,
I'll go and talk to the others.

47:45.404 --> 47:46.738
-Watch over him.
-Sure.

47:46.822 --> 47:48.156
You're his guardian angel.

47:49.616 --> 47:53.328
-Where are you--
-Oh, Bong, you did a really good job.

47:55.789 --> 47:56.999
He's right, you know?

47:57.082 --> 47:59.877
It was pretty amazing, what you did.
I'm impressed.

48:02.296 --> 48:04.172
You promised to watch over me.

48:04.673 --> 48:08.719
Do you realize how scared I was? He put
a knife to my eye, and he took my bag.

48:12.055 --> 48:15.392
Geun-dae, don't cry.
I'm sorry. I'm really sorry.

48:15.475 --> 48:18.061
I promise
I'll never let you out of my sight.

48:18.145 --> 48:20.564
-Bong, I'll protect you forever.
-Just forget it.

48:22.024 --> 48:22.858
Forever?

48:23.942 --> 48:26.361
Why would you
protect me forever, Inspector?

48:27.613 --> 48:29.489
Well, n… not forever.

48:29.573 --> 48:30.908
Uh, more like

48:32.075 --> 48:33.118
forever at work.

48:34.077 --> 48:34.912
All right.

48:34.995 --> 48:38.040
When you were looking for me,
what exactly did you say?

48:38.123 --> 48:40.751
Guy with small, pretty gray eyes
that sparkle?

48:40.834 --> 48:44.421
He looks like a computer geek,
but if you look closely, he's kinda cute.

48:44.922 --> 48:45.923
He's tall,

48:46.423 --> 48:48.216
and he looks super smart.

48:52.387 --> 48:54.932
Yeah, I was just, you know,

48:56.391 --> 48:57.225
describing you.

48:57.309 --> 48:59.603
That's the first time
anyone has said my eyes are small.

48:59.686 --> 49:02.981
Statistically, my eyes are average size
and perfectly adequate.

49:03.482 --> 49:05.651
Have a closer look.
They look small to you?

49:06.485 --> 49:07.319
Huh?

49:10.155 --> 49:11.114
Am I right?

49:14.326 --> 49:16.244
-Wow, look at that.
-What?

49:16.328 --> 49:18.455
I've never been here before.
Wanna take a look?

49:18.538 --> 49:22.042
You can't just change the subject
like that. Just say my eyes aren't small.

49:22.125 --> 49:26.046
-Have you been before? It's so beautiful.
-Why would I ever wanna come here?

49:26.129 --> 49:28.173
Just look at it. Isn't it beautiful?

49:31.093 --> 49:33.136
You're right. You have big eyes.

49:33.220 --> 49:35.055
My eyes aren't big, but they're not small.

49:37.808 --> 49:40.143
-Thank you, sir.
-Please, sit down.

49:40.227 --> 49:41.436
Thank you.

49:46.650 --> 49:49.319
Thanks to you,
my son's health has gotten better.

49:49.403 --> 49:51.363
Good.

49:51.446 --> 49:53.991
But I have been
a very bad father to my son.

49:54.992 --> 49:59.287
I wasn't aware that he had been kidnapped
and beaten like that.

50:00.664 --> 50:04.793
I thought he'd run away from home,
and I blamed him for all the gambling.

50:04.876 --> 50:09.131
You are a good father. You never gave up
on your son, and you came to us for help.

50:09.631 --> 50:12.467
Because of you,
we were able to save him and the others.

50:15.679 --> 50:16.638
Thank you.

50:18.974 --> 50:20.976
I'm very happy he's back home,

50:22.144 --> 50:24.521
but honestly, I'm really worried.

50:25.022 --> 50:26.690
I'm not sure I have the strength anymore.

50:28.316 --> 50:30.402
What if he starts gambling again?

50:33.071 --> 50:35.532
If you were gonna give up,
you would've already done it.

50:35.615 --> 50:37.409
Don't give up on him now.

50:37.909 --> 50:39.745
Continue to believe in him.

50:39.828 --> 50:42.039
That's the only way
you can help him change.

50:45.584 --> 50:47.461
You're not alone anymore.

50:47.544 --> 50:49.671
The Bureau is with you now.

50:50.881 --> 50:52.215
I'm so grateful, sir.

50:58.346 --> 50:59.556
Thank you so much.

51:04.770 --> 51:07.355
I'VE BEEN MAKING FOOLISH MISTAKES
SINCE I STARTED GAMBLING

51:11.735 --> 51:13.278
TEEN GAMBLING COUNSELING FORM

51:23.830 --> 51:25.582
Are you gonna tell him or should I?

51:31.213 --> 51:32.130
Jae-yun,

51:33.006 --> 51:34.966
I know the person who gave you up.

51:36.843 --> 51:37.677
I did.

51:38.762 --> 51:41.890
And I'm also the one
who got you hooked on gambling.

51:42.432 --> 51:45.435
When you stopped doing it,
I used the phone to entice you back.

51:47.229 --> 51:51.691
It's not to get you gambling again. Just
use it for webtoons when you're bored.

51:54.027 --> 51:57.072
You fucking asshole.
How could you do this to me?

51:57.739 --> 52:00.700
We've known each other
ever since elementary school!

52:01.201 --> 52:03.954
-You were supposed to be my friend.
-I had no choice!

52:04.037 --> 52:06.748
They threatened me and my parents.
I had to do it.

52:12.712 --> 52:13.713
Sit down.

52:14.548 --> 52:15.465
Sit down.

52:18.885 --> 52:20.512
Seong-bin, you'll be punished fairly.

52:21.012 --> 52:23.974
You'll either be expelled
or suspended from school.

52:24.516 --> 52:27.018
But you'll also
be facing criminal charges.

52:27.102 --> 52:30.063
If you're lucky,
you might get away with community service.

52:30.147 --> 52:31.439
Otherwise, it's jail.

52:32.691 --> 52:35.610
That's not fair!
This is because of adult criminals.

52:35.694 --> 52:37.946
They threatened us,
and used us to make money!

52:38.029 --> 52:39.573
I'm a victim, too, you know.

52:39.656 --> 52:41.741
What makes you think you're a victim?!

52:43.034 --> 52:44.411
You think you're victims?

52:45.495 --> 52:46.955
What about your parents?

52:47.455 --> 52:49.833
They lost their savings. Their homes.

52:49.916 --> 52:51.418
Some lost their jobs.

52:52.377 --> 52:54.087
All because
of their child's gambling debts.

52:55.714 --> 52:59.217
What about the father who is assaulted
and beaten up in front of his colleagues

52:59.301 --> 53:00.510
by a thug half his age?

53:03.013 --> 53:06.016
The father who has to kneel and beg
so he can save his son?

53:09.936 --> 53:12.731
What about the mother
who takes a job in a restaurant,

53:12.814 --> 53:15.609
scrubbing and washing dirty dishes,
trying to make some money

53:15.692 --> 53:18.778
because the father quit his job
to watch over their son?

53:25.785 --> 53:29.122
What about the father who is
ignored and tossed aside by the police,

53:29.206 --> 53:33.793
treated like some homeless beggar by
the administration and the ERPB and yet…

53:33.877 --> 53:36.213
and yet he never stops trying.

53:36.296 --> 53:38.632
Never gives up his only objective.

53:39.132 --> 53:40.342
To save his son.

53:48.808 --> 53:49.893
Think about that.

53:52.979 --> 53:55.106
The real victims here are your parents.

54:01.446 --> 54:04.824
You've had numerous chances
to stop gambling, but you didn't.

54:06.076 --> 54:08.787
That choice was yours.
You're responsible for that.

54:13.500 --> 54:15.210
Do you really wanna stop?

54:15.293 --> 54:17.629
Do you want to be forgiven
by your families?

54:18.880 --> 54:20.840
Then, from now on, live honestly.

54:23.301 --> 54:25.804
Take the time
to contemplate what you've done,

54:27.097 --> 54:29.015
and to ask forgiveness of others.

54:32.477 --> 54:34.604
Because this will be your last chance.

54:48.451 --> 54:52.414
Your eyes

54:52.497 --> 54:56.584
Still glowing

54:57.210 --> 55:01.589
Just like the day we met…

55:01.673 --> 55:03.258
Here. This'll help.

55:03.883 --> 55:05.343
Hot, isn't it?

55:05.427 --> 55:08.096
Your eyes…

55:08.179 --> 55:09.306
And it works.

55:09.389 --> 55:11.891
Still holding…

55:11.975 --> 55:13.810
Forget about get-rich-quick scams.

55:13.893 --> 55:16.771
Money is earned
through hard, honest labor like that.

55:17.647 --> 55:19.232
Scrub, scrub and scrub.

55:19.858 --> 55:22.068
-You're washing your souls clean.
-You missed a spot.

55:22.652 --> 55:23.737
Hand it over.

55:26.698 --> 55:28.450
Thank you. Hm.

55:30.869 --> 55:36.708
Based on my calculations,
you now owe your parents 98,300,020 won.

55:37.208 --> 55:38.960
This is your mess. You clean it up.

55:39.044 --> 55:40.295
Before I forget…

55:43.381 --> 55:45.675
To page, press one. To record a message…

55:47.719 --> 55:51.723
These are your pagers. I hope you still
remember what those numbers mean?

55:51.806 --> 55:53.058
I love you. Come quickly.

55:53.933 --> 55:56.728
-Remember that.
-So, can we have our phones back now?

55:56.811 --> 55:58.063
Just to make calls.

55:58.146 --> 56:00.190
There's no one at school that uses those.

56:00.273 --> 56:03.151
A wise man once said,
"Freedom comes with responsibility."

56:03.234 --> 56:07.155
And another wise man said,
"Never trust the promise of a gambler."

56:07.864 --> 56:09.032
I'll page you guys.

56:10.116 --> 56:11.951
143143.

56:17.207 --> 56:18.583
I told you, it's fine.

56:18.666 --> 56:21.461
I'm the reason that your phone
broke in the first place.

56:21.544 --> 56:25.131
It's only the screen that's broken.
The phone can still be used.

56:27.217 --> 56:28.343
I'm feeling guilty.

56:28.426 --> 56:32.097
I said that I'd protect you,
but, in the end, I failed.

56:32.597 --> 56:33.932
So do me a favor.

56:34.015 --> 56:35.016
Pick a new phone.

56:35.517 --> 56:38.061
-You can choose whichever one you want.
-Honestly, it's fine.

56:38.144 --> 56:39.979
-Go! Pick the latest model.
-Wait…

56:41.731 --> 56:43.858
This one here,
I'll just take a peek, okay?

56:45.110 --> 56:46.903
-You like this one?
-Yeah.

56:46.986 --> 56:51.199
This is their new model, with a CPU that's
superfast, which means faster internet.

56:51.282 --> 56:52.367
-Pretty cool.
-Hm.

56:52.450 --> 56:54.244
-You see?
-Mm.

56:56.121 --> 56:57.288
Huh?

57:15.557 --> 57:17.225
Do you have any flip phones for sale?

57:17.308 --> 57:19.102
-We don't need a flip phone.
-Yes, we do.

57:19.185 --> 57:22.188
No, seriously, I don't gamble anymore.
I'm not addicted.

57:22.272 --> 57:24.107
Yes, I've found another addict.
I'm on my way.

57:24.190 --> 57:25.400
I swear I stopped gambling.

57:25.483 --> 57:27.444
-Sir, yes sir!
-Bye, have a nice day.

57:27.527 --> 57:28.653
Ah, nice to meet you.

57:28.736 --> 57:29.946
Cheese!

57:30.029 --> 57:33.741
Hwang Gi-tae! Hwang Gi-tae! Hwang Gi-tae!

57:34.451 --> 57:37.620
-Ah, very beautiful, thank you.
-Please, have some tea. Careful, it's hot.

57:37.704 --> 57:39.289
In the latest poll,

57:39.372 --> 57:42.542
Minister Choi Gang-seok surpassed
the 50% approval mark,

57:42.625 --> 57:45.837
leading opposition leader
Hwang Gi-tae by 17%.

57:45.920 --> 57:48.548
As Minister Choi Gang-seok
maintains a commanding lead,

57:48.631 --> 57:50.467
whether he will enter
the presidential race

57:50.550 --> 57:52.969
has become the hottest question
in political circles.

57:53.052 --> 57:54.512
-This way, sir.
-Thank you.

57:54.596 --> 57:56.347
Thank you, Mr. Hwang, for visiting us.

57:56.431 --> 57:58.433
Thank you very much. Thank you.

57:59.100 --> 58:01.519
So you've already
started campaigning, I see.

58:02.187 --> 58:03.730
Is that Minister Choi Gang-seok?

58:04.981 --> 58:07.358
Come, join me. I'm a regular here.

58:08.318 --> 58:10.737
Excuse me? Can you bring us another stew?

58:10.820 --> 58:13.072
Thank you.
No photos. Just a moment, please.

58:16.201 --> 58:17.076
Hm.

58:23.458 --> 58:24.334
Hm.

58:24.834 --> 58:28.713
Strange that you're campaigning
when you're not officially a candidate,

58:29.339 --> 58:31.799
and the election campaign
has not yet begun.

58:32.300 --> 58:34.844
-This looks really delicious.
-I hope you like it.

58:36.095 --> 58:38.181
So, Minister, have you been
listening to the news?

58:38.264 --> 58:39.641
Ah!

58:40.308 --> 58:43.061
Then again, you're not the kind
who listens to rumors.

58:45.480 --> 58:47.857
The word in the House of Congress is that

58:49.651 --> 58:52.529
you're using the murder of your daughter
to help your career.

58:53.655 --> 58:55.907
Using her death to run for president.

58:59.202 --> 59:00.495
Hm.

59:10.171 --> 59:12.340
I see you like
keeping up to date on rumors.

59:12.924 --> 59:16.010
So I guess you heard that the party
is holding an emergency meeting today.

59:18.137 --> 59:19.681
Maybe you haven't heard?

59:20.181 --> 59:22.308
What did they need to discuss

59:23.226 --> 59:25.478
that required keeping you in the dark?

59:28.815 --> 59:31.776
Considering that your approval ratings
are so low,

59:31.859 --> 59:34.821
maybe they're planning
on finding a new candidate.

59:39.617 --> 59:41.119
Who's behind this?

59:41.202 --> 59:43.288
I'm heading down there right now!

59:45.081 --> 59:47.709
They cannot stop me.
I'm the leader of the party!

59:47.792 --> 59:49.294
Do you hear what I said?

59:51.337 --> 59:52.171
What?

59:54.382 --> 59:56.092
My apologies, sir, but you have a visitor.

59:56.175 --> 59:58.219
Do I look like
I'm in the mood for visitors?!

59:58.886 --> 01:00:02.890
He says he has some important information
for you about the ERPB.
